# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work

.env
# Exclude local SQlite DB user for local testing
test.db
test.sqlite

.DS_Store

website/dist/*
website-experiment/dist/*
website-experiment/node_modules/
website-experiment/test-results/
website-experiment/playwright-report/

# Temp worker directory, and local scratch copies of it.
#
# Anchored to the repository root. Unanchored, `worker` matches *any* path
# component of that name -- which silently excluded the whole of `pkg/worker`
# when the NATS worker was extracted into a package, in a way that shows up only
# as a missing package in CI.
/worker/
/worker.*
